WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:04.110
2022 and 2026.

2
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.210
What changed?

3
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.800
And how did Data Lucas read
the night of the count?

4
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:16.422
In 2022, Lula beat Jair
Bolsonaro by 2.1 million votes.

5
00:00:16.462 --> 00:00:20.910
In 2026, against Flávio
Bolsonaro, his lead doubled:

6
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.125
4.4 million.

7
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:31.047
Lula gained in 16 states
and lost ground in 11.

8
00:00:31.087 --> 00:00:32.922
Amapá swung to Lula;

9
00:00:32.962 --> 00:00:35.137
Tocantins, to Flávio.

10
00:00:41.783 --> 00:00:44.005
In the cities, a paradox.

11
00:00:44.045 --> 00:00:47.881
Lula lost ground in most municipalities,
but grew in the large ones:

12
00:00:47.921 --> 00:00:51.433
he gained in 73 of the 75 largest.

13
00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:00.397
From the first to the second
round, almost 13% more votes.

14
00:01:00.437 --> 00:01:04.250
And the more a city turned
out, the more Lula grew.

15
00:01:08.817 --> 00:01:11.089
Abroad, Lula also gained:

16
00:01:11.129 --> 00:01:13.955
from 51% to 53%.

17
00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.760
As the votes were
counted, the tally swung.

18
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.685
With 7% of polling sections
counted, the panel predicted:

19
00:01:24.725 --> 00:01:29.048
Flávio would take the lead, and
Lula would regain it near 40%.

20
00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:32.835
That is what happened, at 14% and 47%.

21
00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:34.872
And the projection never moved:

22
00:01:34.912 --> 00:01:36.124
always Lula.

23
00:01:40.683 --> 00:01:44.868
With 2% of sections counted, the
projection was off by less than one point.

24
00:01:44.908 --> 00:01:47.056
At the end, by two hundredths of a point.

25
00:01:47.096 --> 00:01:52.008
In all 144 rounds, the result
stayed within the margin.

26
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.160
The polls had Lula losing.

27
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:04.560
Data Lucas called Lula the winner
with only 2.7% of sections counted.

28
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.337
At 8%, it was decided.

29
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:13.133
Data Lucas.
